@format 1
@id section-creation.set-end-creates-section
@title Set End creates a section
@section Section creation
@area In Split tab
@entry end-dispatch
@summary Follow only the Set End branch that creates a new section when no section is selected; changing an existing section end is outside this map.
@related section-creation.common.compass-buttons, section-creation.common.keyboard-shortcuts, section-creation.common.apply-created-state
@tag section
@tag split
@tag creation
@tag end

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias piece = Cadroue.Core.LPiece

[end-dispatch] setEnd dispatch request <input>
~ This starts with setEnd dispatch request.
[Technical explanation]
= The request came from the Split Compass End button or the currently bound SectionEnd shortcut.
> dispatch-guard

[dispatch-guard] Active Split flow guard <decision>
~ The program checks active Split flow guard.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowShortcutDispatch requires a command-active flow with a loaded spool and active section UI before invoking PFlowEndSet @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setEnd
? "Rejected" > dispatch-rejected
? "Accepted" > end-handler

[dispatch-rejected] Set End command ignored <output>
~ This path ends with set End command ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= No section operation is called.

[end-handler] Set End creation preconditions <decision>
~ The program checks set End creation preconditions.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowEndSet requires section editing to be enabled plus a spool and nonblank source path, then chooses the color from current section count modulo active palette count and calls LSegmentEndSet with cursor, color, and overlap policy @ flow.PFlowEndSet(...)
@ flow.PFlowColorRead(...)
@ property flow.PFlowOverlapAllowed
? "Editing disabled or media/source unavailable" > end-rejected
? "Preconditions accepted" > selection-check

[end-rejected] Set End creation blocked <output>
~ This path ends with set End creation blocked.
[Technical explanation]
= No section state changes.

[selection-check] Is a section already selected? <decision>
~ Is a section already selected?
[Technical explanation]
- LSegmentEndSet delegates to LPieceEndSet; only a null active index enters LPieceEndCreate, while a selected section enters the existing-section end path @ segment.LSegmentEndSet(...)
@ piece.LPieceEndSet(...)
? "Section selected" > existing-end-outside
? "No section selected" > cursor-check

[existing-end-outside] Existing-section end path excluded <output>
~ This path ends with existing-section end path excluded.
[Technical explanation]
= Editing or rejecting the selected section's end is outside the requested creation-only scope.

[cursor-check] End cursor after zero <decision>
~ The program checks end cursor after zero.
[Technical explanation]
- LPieceEndCreate rejects a cursor at or before zero @ piece.LPieceEndCreate(...)
? "Cursor at or before zero" > zero-rejected
? "Cursor after zero" > floor-read

[zero-rejected] No section plan <output>
~ This path ends with no section plan.
[Technical explanation]
= No new section is created.

[floor-read] Determine the new section start <process>
~ This step handles determine the new section start.
[Technical explanation]
- LPieceFloorRead returns zero when overlap is allowed; otherwise it returns the latest existing section end that is not later than the cursor @ piece.LPieceFloorRead(...)
> floor-check

[floor-check] Positive span from start to cursor <decision>
~ The program checks positive span from start to cursor.
[Technical explanation]
- LPieceEndCreate requires the computed start to be earlier than the cursor @ piece.LPieceEndCreate(...) / start check
? "Start is not earlier" > floor-rejected
? "Start is earlier" > obstruction-check

[floor-rejected] No section plan because span is empty <output>
~ This path ends with no section plan because span is empty.
[Technical explanation]
= No new section is created.

[obstruction-check] No intervening blocked span <decision>
~ The program checks no intervening blocked span.
[Technical explanation]
- When overlap is disabled, LPieceLimitRead detects a section start between the computed start and cursor; LPieceEndCreate rejects if the cursor passes that limit @ piece.LPieceLimitRead(...)
@ piece.LPieceEndCreate(...) / limit check
? "Blocked before cursor" > obstruction-rejected
? "Clear to cursor" > end-plan

[obstruction-rejected] No section plan because another section intervenes <output>
~ This path ends with no section plan because another section intervenes.
[Technical explanation]
= No new section is created.

[end-plan] Append a new unnamed ending section <process>
~ This step handles append a new unnamed ending section.
[Technical explanation]
- Append LPiece(computed start, cursor, color index, empty name), select the new last index, and return Added=true to LSegmentEndSet @ piece.LPieceEndCreate(...)
@ piece.LPieceEndSet(...) / Added true creation result
> map:section-creation.common.apply-created-state
